<section class="page-hero">
  <div id="ambient-canvas" class="ambient-canvas"></div>
  <div class="container page-hero-inner">
    <span class="eyebrow">Free Tool</span>
    <h1>Free llms.txt Generator</h1>
    <p>Create a valid <code>llms.txt</code> file in seconds — a plain-language map of your site that helps ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, and other AI assistants understand and cite your business correctly.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container contact-grid llms-tool-grid">
    <div>
      <form class="contact-form llms-form" id="llms-form" onsubmit="return false;">
        <div>
          <label for="lt-name">Site or company name</label>
          <input type="text" id="lt-name" placeholder="Acme Roofing Co.">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="lt-summary">One-line summary</label>
          <input type="text" id="lt-summary" placeholder="Acme Roofing Co. installs and repairs residential roofs across Austin, TX.">
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="lt-description">Longer description (optional)</label>
          <textarea id="lt-description" placeholder="A short paragraph with any context an AI assistant should know — history, specialties, service area, or anything that helps it describe you accurately."></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="lt-pages">Key pages — one per line: <code>Label | URL | Description</code></label>
          <textarea id="lt-pages" placeholder="Roof Repair | https://example.com/roof-repair | Emergency and scheduled roof repair&#10;About Us | https://example.com/about | Company history and service area&#10;Contact | https://example.com/contact | Get a free quote"></textarea>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="lt-optional">Optional / secondary pages (optional) — same format</label>
          <textarea id="lt-optional" placeholder="Careers | https://example.com/careers | Open positions&#10;Blog | https://example.com/blog | Roofing tips and guides"></textarea>
        </div>
      </form>
    </div>

    <div class="contact-info-card llms-preview-card">
      <div class="llms-preview-head">
        <strong>llms.txt preview</strong>
        <span id="lt-status" class="llms-status">Fill in the form to generate</span>
      </div>
      <pre id="lt-output" class="llms-output"># Your llms.txt will appear here</pre>
      <div class="llms-actions">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm" id="lt-copy">Copy</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" id="lt-download">Download llms.txt</button>
      </div>
      <p class="llms-hint">Upload the downloaded file to your site's root directory so it's reachable at <code>yoursite.com/llms.txt</code>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="container llms-explainer">
    <h2>What is llms.txt?</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-dim);"><code>llms.txt</code> is a plain-text file, written in simple Markdown, that sits at the root of your domain (like <code>robots.txt</code> or <code>sitemap.xml</code>) and gives AI assistants a short, structured summary of who you are and where your most important pages live. Unlike a sitemap, it isn't a crawl directive — it's a hand-written cheat sheet that helps an AI model describe your business accurately instead of guessing from whatever page it happens to land on.</p>

    <h2>Why it matters for AI search</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-dim);">As more people ask ChatGPT, Claude, and Perplexity for recommendations instead of typing a Google query, being described correctly by those tools matters as much as ranking well in search results. See our guide to <a href="/blog/what-is-llm-seo-2026">LLM SEO</a> for the bigger picture, and <a href="/blog/how-to-get-cited-by-chatgpt-2026">how to get cited by ChatGPT</a> for what to do once your llms.txt is live.</p>

    <h2>How to add it to your site</h2>
    <ul class="service-points">
      <li>Fill in the form above and click Download</li>
      <li>Rename the file to exactly <code>llms.txt</code> if your browser changed the name</li>
      <li>Upload it to your site's root directory (the same place <code>robots.txt</code> lives)</li>
      <li>Confirm it loads at <code>https://yoursite.com/llms.txt</code></li>
      <li>Update it whenever your key pages or offerings change</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Free llms.txt Generator FAQs</h2>
    <div class="faq-list" style="margin-top: 22px;">
      <details>
        <summary>Is llms.txt the same as robots.txt?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. robots.txt tells crawlers which pages they're allowed to access. llms.txt doesn't control access at all — it's a plain-language summary that helps AI assistants understand and describe your site once they've read it.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Do I need to know how to code to add this?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No. Download the generated file and upload it to your site's root folder using your host's file manager or FTP client — the same place your <code>robots.txt</code> or <code>favicon.ico</code> already lives.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Will this guarantee ChatGPT or Claude mentions my business?<span class="faq-icon"></span></summary>
        <p>No tool can guarantee that. llms.txt is still an emerging, voluntary convention that not every AI system reads yet — but it costs nothing to add and gives the ones that do read it accurate information instead of a guess.</p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How often should I update my llms.txt file?</summary>
        <p>Whenever your key pages, services, or offerings change meaningfully — there's no fixed schedule, treat it like your sitemap or meta description.</p>
      </details>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-band" style="margin-top: 44px;">
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-1"></span>
      <span class="cta-orb cta-orb-2"></span>
      <h2>Want help beyond a single file?</h2>
      <p>Contomatix builds full LLM SEO and AI-visibility strategies, not just the basics.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact" class="btn btn-primary">Get in touch</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/<%= site.whatsappNumber %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-glass">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script type="application/ld+json">
  <%- JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebApplication',
    name: 'Free llms.txt Generator',
    url: site.baseUrl + '/tools/llms-txt-generator',
    applicationCategory: 'BusinessApplication',
    operatingSystem: 'Any (browser-based)',
    offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
    description: 'Generate a valid llms.txt file for free — a plain-language summary of your site for ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity and other AI assistants.',
    provider: { '@id': site.baseUrl + '/#organization' }
  }) %>
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
  <%- JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is llms.txt the same as robots.txt?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "No. robots.txt tells crawlers which pages they're allowed to access. llms.txt doesn't control access at all — it's a plain-language summary that helps AI assistants understand and describe your site once they've read it." } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Do I need to know how to code to add this?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "No. Download the generated file and upload it to your site's root folder using your host's file manager or FTP client — the same place your robots.txt or favicon.ico already lives." } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Will this guarantee ChatGPT or Claude mentions my business?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No tool can guarantee that. llms.txt is still an emerging, voluntary convention that not every AI system reads yet — but it costs nothing to add and gives the ones that do read it accurate information instead of a guess.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How often should I update my llms.txt file?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: "Whenever your key pages, services, or offerings change meaningfully — there's no fixed schedule, treat it like your sitemap or meta description." } }
    ]
  }) %>
</script>

<script>
(function () {
  function parseRows(text) {
    return text.split('\n').map(function (line) { return line.trim(); }).filter(Boolean).map(function (line) {
      var parts = line.split('|').map(function (p) { return p.trim(); });
      return { label: parts[0] || '', url: parts[1] || '', desc: parts[2] || '' };
    });
  }

  function rowsToMarkdown(rows) {
    return rows.filter(function (r) { return r.label && r.url; }).map(function (r) {
      return '- [' + r.label + '](' + r.url + ')' + (r.desc ? ': ' + r.desc : '');
    }).join('\n');
  }

  function build() {
    var name = document.getElementById('lt-name').value.trim();
    var summary = document.getElementById('lt-summary').value.trim();
    var description = document.getElementById('lt-description').value.trim();
    var pages = rowsToMarkdown(parseRows(document.getElementById('lt-pages').value));
    var optional = rowsToMarkdown(parseRows(document.getElementById('lt-optional').value));

    if (!name) {
      document.getElementById('lt-output').textContent = '# Your llms.txt will appear here';
      document.getElementById('lt-status').textContent = 'Fill in the form to generate';
      return '';
    }

    var out = '# ' + name + '\n';
    if (summary) out += '\n> ' + summary + '\n';
    if (description) out += '\n' + description + '\n';
    if (pages) out += '\n## Pages\n\n' + pages + '\n';
    if (optional) out += '\n## Optional\n\n' + optional + '\n';

    document.getElementById('lt-output').textContent = out.trim() + '\n';
    document.getElementById('lt-status').textContent = 'Updated';
    return out.trim() + '\n';
  }

  ['lt-name', 'lt-summary', 'lt-description', 'lt-pages', 'lt-optional'].forEach(function (id) {
    document.getElementById(id).addEventListener('input', build);
  });

  document.getElementById('lt-copy').addEventListener('click', function () {
    var text = document.getElementById('lt-output').textContent;
    if (!text || text.indexOf('will appear here') !== -1) return;
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(function () {
      var status = document.getElementById('lt-status');
      status.textContent = 'Copied!';
      setTimeout(function () { status.textContent = 'Updated'; }, 1800);
    });
  });

  document.getElementById('lt-download').addEventListener('click', function () {
    var text = document.getElementById('lt-output').textContent;
    if (!text || text.indexOf('will appear here') !== -1) return;
    var blob = new Blob([text], { type: 'text/plain' });
    var url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
    var a = document.createElement('a');
    a.href = url;
    a.download = 'llms.txt';
    document.body.appendChild(a);
    a.click();
    document.body.removeChild(a);
    URL.revokeObjectURL(url);
  });
})();
</script>
